          "statement": "OT cybersecurity must be managed with OT-specific performance, reliability, availability, and safety constraints. IACS may include SIS; cyber threats to programmable IACS can cause undetected faults, failure, downtime, and increased major-accident risk, and interfaces or shared dependencies must be considered when assessing protective-system independence. Safety-related software and relevant development/configuration tools and modifications remain within the applicable functional-safety lifecycle controls. NIST SSDF guidance explicitly does not distinguish human-written from AI-generated source code for pre-use vulnerability evaluation. Applying those controls to AI-generated safety code is an inference from the software scope and secure-development guidance, not an AI-specific IEC 61508/61511 requirement; verification rigor and independent assessment follow the applicable SIL, complexity, and safety plan.",
